Ports Every DevOps Engineer Should Know 💡

Whether you're setting up a CI/CD pipeline, deploying monitoring tools, or configuring cloud-native apps, knowing the default ports of key services is non-negotiable. Here's a quick reference for some of the most commonly used tools and technologies:

🛠️ DevOps & CI/CD

Jenkins → 8080

SonarQube → 9000

Docker → 2375, 2376

Kubernetes API Server → 6443

Kubelet → 10250


📊 Monitoring & Visualization

Prometheus → 9090

Grafana → 3000

Alertmanager → 9093

Node Exporter → 9100

Blackbox Exporter → 9112


🌐 Web & App Servers

Tomcat → 8080

Apache / Nginx / HTTP → 80

HTTPS → 443

React.js / Node.js → 3000

Python (dev server) → 8000


📡 Networking & Communication

FTP → 21

SSH → 22

SMTP (SSL) → 465

DNS → 53

Ngrok Dashboard → 4040


🗃️ Databases

MySQL → 3306

PostgreSQL → 5432

Redis → 6379


📦 Logging & Search

Logstash → 5044

Elasticsearch → 9200

Kibana → 5601


📡 Streaming & Messaging

Kafka → 9092
